# O8d (the bulk review's F6): an extern call lets go of anything where C may call an export fn that lets go - a view held
# across one keeps what it names; and a program with an export fn frees nothing early (condition 3)
import "std/io"

extern link "callback.o" {
    fn c_run(i I64)
}

type Holder struct() {
    t String& = ""
}

G mut Holder& = Holder()

# C calls this by its name: it lets go of the global holder's text
export fn olang_reset(i I64) {
    G.t = $"text number " $i " padded out to many bytes ........................................"
}

fn churn() I64 {
    t I64 = 0
    for i in range 300 {
        a := Array<I64>(64, -7)
        t += a[3]
        s := $i $i $i "-" $(i * 7) " some more text to fill the chunk ......"
        t += s.Len()
    }
    return t
}

fn main() {
    olang_reset(-1)
    for i in range 5 {
        v := G.t            # a view of the global holder's text
        c_run(i)            # C calls olang_reset, which lets go of it
        churn()
        io.Println(v)!
    }
}
